#====================================================================
# DRAFT-au-0.6.0-ohos-mpil-powl-float-tests
# 触发事件: au 0.6.0 HarmonyOS PC 适配（R01 上游测试）
#          Pi/GetValue 两测试因 M_PIl 缺失无条件失败;
#          Root 测试因 OHOS powl 相对误差 ~1e-15 超 gtest DoubleEq 容差
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-au-0.6.0-ohos-mpil-powl-float-tests
trigger_tool:           au|gtest|gmock|clang|ctest|libm|powl|cmake
phase:                  testing|verification|porting
error_signature: 'M_PIl not available on this architecture|Expected: is approximately 384173749\.49624783|ResultIsVeryCloseToStdPowForPureRoots'

severity:               2
category:               ohos|portability|upstream-test|long-double|float-comparison|gtest
match_keywords:         OHOS, M_PIl, long double, powl, gtest, DoubleEq,
                         relative tolerance, float comparison, pi constant,
                         root, std::pow, upstream test, clang-15, aarch64

title: 'OHOS upstream float tests: missing M_PIl constant and powl error beyond gtest DoubleEq'

root_cause: >
  Two independent platform test-portability issues on OHOS aarch64 / clang-15:
  (1) The OHOS libc (musl-based) headers do not define M_PIl, and upstream tests
  written with `#ifdef M_PIl ... #else ADD_FAILURE()` fail unconditionally when
  ported (Pi.HasCorrectValue, GetValue.PiToThePower1HasCorrectValues).
  (2) OHOS libm std::pow(long double) carries roughly 1e-15 relative error in the
  ordinary double domain; au's own root() binary search in 128-bit quad long double
  is closer to the true value (au error 2.3e-08 vs powl error 4.5e-07 for the cube
  root of 5.67e25), so comparing au value against the powl reference with gtest
  DoubleEq (4*DBL_EPSILON ~8.9e-16 relative) fails even though the library is correct.

solution: >
  (1) Define a portable long double pi constant
  `constexpr long double kPiLongDouble = 3.141592653589793238462643383279502884L;`
  (same value as glibc M_PIl) and compare against it in the #else branch instead
  of ADD_FAILURE().
  (2) Replace `DoubleEq(std::pow(x, 1.0L/r))` with
  `DoubleNear(expected, kRelativeTolerance * |expected|)` using a 1e-12 relative
  tolerance, after quantifying absdiff/rel diff. Do not delete or weaken tests
  arbitrarily; library source code stays untouched.

verification_cmd: >
  ctest --test-dir build-cmake -j1 --output-on-failure
  (au 0.6.0 R01: 1824/1824 = 100% after the two test portability fixes;
  probe sizeof(long double)=16 quad; char signed=0 on arm64)

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           portable-pi-constant-plus-relative-tolerance
rec_description:        Replace missing M_PIl with an equivalent long double literal
                        and relax overly strict DoubleEq comparisons against OHOS powl
                        to a documented relative tolerance (1e-12), keeping assertions
                        meaningful and library code unchanged.
rec_auto_fix:           true
rec_impl:               test-portability-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      document-platform-difference-only
fallback_description:   If patching upstream tests is not acceptable, record the two
                        failures as platform reference-oracle differences (M_PIl absent,
                        powl error) in the ledger without changing assertions.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          ledger-only

forbid_1_pattern:       ADD_FAILURE.*M_PIl|gtest_filter.*Pi|exclude.*Root
forbid_1_reason:        Disabling or filtering the failing tests hides platform
                        portability evidence and is not a fix.
forbid_2_pattern:       DoubleEq.*1e-12|abs\(.*-.*\).*<.*1e-3
forbid_2_reason:        Arbitrarily loosening tolerances without quantification
                        masks real library regressions on other platforms.

related:                DRAFT-gcem-1.16.0-ohos-libm-long-double-boundary
similar_to:             gcem-1.16.0-ohos-libm-long-double-boundary
path:                   B (knowledge extension; new differences vs existing knowledge)
dedup:                  doc/ miss; graph/ miss; drafts/ partial (gcem boundary,
                        different root cause/entry); error-patterns miss
affected_scope:         OHOS aarch64 C/C++ libs whose upstream tests consume M_PIl
                        or assert strict float equality against libm powl references
verification_evidence:  ctest 1824/1824=100%; magnitude_test 3 fixed tests PASS;
                        powl vs au root probe numbers in ledger/report
pr_prefix:              【知识库扩展】
